`--target` is for cross-compilation targets (e.g. `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`). The correct flag for output directory is `--target-dir`:

```powershell
cargo run --bin testhandler --target-dir D:\target_rs_build -- "Test query with fastembed"
```

Or for release:
```powershell
cargo build --release --target-dir D:\target_rs_build
D:\target_rs_build\release\testhandler.exe "Test query with fastembed"
```

Since we already created [C:\Users\thinkpad123\TCPNRS\DEV_ISTA\rag_system\.cargo\config.toml](cci:7://file:///C:/Users/thinkpad123/TCPNRS/DEV_ISTA/rag_system/.cargo/config.toml:0:0-0:0) with:
```toml
[build]
target-dir = "D:\\target_rs_build"
```

You can just run **without any extra flags** from the `rag_system` directory:
```powershell
cd C:\Users\thinkpad123\TCPNRS\DEV_ISTA\rag_system\rag
cargo build --release
D:\target_rs_build\release\testhandler.exe "Test query with fastembed"
```

The config.toml handles the target dir automatically.



